<title>USA: Jaguar April U.S. vehicle sales up 14 pct.</title>
<headline>Jaguar April U.S. vehicle sales up 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MAHWAH, N.J. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jaguar Cars, a wholly owned subsidiary of Ford Motor Co, said its U.S. car sales in April rose 14 percent from the same month a year ago to 1,522 cars from 1,335 cars last year.</p>
<p>For the year-to-date, U.S. vehicle sales increased 23.5 percent to 6,026 from 4,878 cars, Jaquar said in a statement.</p>
<p>		   ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
